From 6867f9cf74554c9b3b5c7d1c01fd17cb3dc8b5fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Pukhov <alex.m.pukhov@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:57:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Rectilinear meshes (gridCoordinates, openPMD-standard #142)

Meshes with explicit, non-equidistant coordinates along some axes: the
attribute gridCoordinates (on the component or the record) names a 1D
coordinate data set per axis ('' = regular axis).

- FieldMetaInformation: optional grid_coordinates; along such axes x (etc.)
  are the positions of the data points, dx the smallest spacing; new
  attribute rectilinear (list of axes) and get_edges(label) for plotting
- both backends (h5py, openpmd-api if it supports grid coordinates) read
  the coordinates, also the interim attributes gridCoordinates_<label> and
  the interim marking geometry 'other' + geometryParameters 'thetaMode;...'
- slicing along a rectilinear axis refers to the coordinate range
- thetaMode 3D reconstruction interpolates between the explicit radial
  nodes (construct_3d_from_circ_rectilinear)
- grid ranges from the coordinates; 2D plots with pcolormesh
- tests/test_rectilinear.py (files written with h5py, every backend)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DRiRr7s6YoyWRd6EM8Zzbz
